WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
Let’s talk about Israel taking over the West Bank.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.280
They’ve occupied it for decades.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.080
The difference this time is Israel wants to make it official.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.200
But Palestinians call it an illegal land grab.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.920
The Arab League, most European countries

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.600
and the United Nations are against it too.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.280
So what would annexation mean for people

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.040
in the occupied West Bank?

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.320
What’s in it for Israel?

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.840
And what does the US election have to do with it?

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.480
When it comes to understanding news

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.760
out of Israel and Palestine it helps to look at a map.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.200
The fact that the map changes all the time

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.600
well that’s part of the problem.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.800
Here’s what it looks like today.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.680
This part is considered Israel.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.040
The Gaza Strip and the West Bank 

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.120
are under Palestinian control.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.560
The real power, though, lies with Israel.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.200
Those Palestinian territories are under

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.640
an Israeli military occupation.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.960
And it’s Israel that decides who and what goes in or out

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.600
and a whole lot more.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.760
And this arrangement is considered illegal

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.600
under international law.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.920
Now the map hasn’t always looked like this.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.760
This was Palestine before 1948.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.080
Over time Israel expanded by winning wars

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.880
moving borders and building settlements.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.160
The focus right now is the occupied West Bank.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:49.080
In more than 50 years Israel’s built at least 250 settlements.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.800
They’re home to more than 600,000 Israeli settlers.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.560
And all those compounds are connected by roads

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.960
that only Israelis can use.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.720
It means Palestinians are trapped

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.440
on a patchwork of land

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.680
blocked by Israeli separation walls

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.960
and with limited freedom to travel.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.440
They have to get through Israeli military checkpoints.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.560
And now Israel wants to annex some of that territory

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.400
meaning it will extend its sovereignty

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.000
over land it already occupies. 

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.320
Now it’s unclear which parts

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.960
the Israeli government is eyeing.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.880
But it could be as much as 30% of the West Bank

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.520
including the Jordan Valley.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.760
Maybe more.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.280
And the Palestinians see that only one way.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.240
Let’s understand what life is already like for Palestinians

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.480
living in the West Bank.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.160
So what will annexation change?

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.800
Well, some Palestinians say — not a lot.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:34.720
But others think life for them is going to get much harder.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.920
They fear more evictions.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:55.200
More Palestinians displaced, and even fewer rights.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.520
One of the biggest concerns for Palestinians

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.840
is the annexation of the Jordan Valley.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.400
It’ll give the Israeli military a strategic vantage point.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.720
Full view and control over the area

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.640
plus total access to the Jordan River.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:28.640
It also means surrounding Palestinian territories

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:32.680
in the West Bank and cutting off their access to water.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.360
Palestinian farmers in the West Bank

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.920
say they barely get enough water as it is.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.720
Israeli settlers in the Jordan Valley

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:54.040
receive almost 20 times more water than they do.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:57.120
All of these issues risk upsetting Israel’s neighbours.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.200
Like Jordan.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.800
So what’s Israel’s justification?

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.720
Well, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.760
doesn’t even call it annexation.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:20.360
He calls it applying sovereignty

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:21.760
over Jewish settlements.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:23.920
It’s something he’s always wanted to do.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.920
He’s made it a campaign promise

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.440
in the last three elections.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.320
But it’s not just Netanyahu.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.960
The Israeli position has always been that the country

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.480
faces the threat of attack

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:40.960
and that the land they’re taking is historically theirs.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.720
Practically speaking annexation also

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:06.200
makes it easier to build more settlements.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.320
Usually it’s Israel’s defence ministry

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:09.960
which approves construction.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.680
But if Israel treats occupied West Bank land

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.280
as its own settlement construction would boil down

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.080
to local paperwork.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.280
All these plans were supposed to go ahead in July.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.120
But they’re on hold for lots of reasons.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.360
The details about annexation still haven’t been worked out.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.720
And Netanyahu’s coalition partner Benny Gantz

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.560
says he’d rather focus on fighting the coronavirus

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:41.880
for now at least.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.960
Even the Americans want more discussion.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:47.880
But there’s no question they’re onside.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:57.680
In fact annexation is part of the Trump administration’s

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:00.400
plan for the region, what the president calls

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.320
his deal of the century.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.920
Jared Kushner — his son-in-law and senior adviser

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.120
drew up the blueprint he says offers a two-state solution

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:12.080
for Israelis and Palestinians to live side by side.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:18.280
But the Palestinians weren’t consulted.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:19.600
And they’re not buying it.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.520
The plan promises a future Palestinian state

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:26.440
in exchange for Israel annexing

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:28.800
large parts of the West Bank.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.120
The Palestinians rejected the deal then …

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:40.440
… and they still do now.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:48.920
There’s also a US presidential election in the mix.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.240
That’s in November.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.680
And plenty of analysts say Prime Minister Netanyahu

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:56.400
is trying to seal the deal in case Trump is voted out.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.840
The challenge will be to maintain that momentum

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:06.120
in the face of nearly universal condemnation.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.480
Even some Israeli settlers aren’t happy with annexation.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:16.640
But for different reasons.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:18.440
Because Trump’s Middle East plan

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:21.080
gives the Palestinians a state their own

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:23.000
no matter how small and disjointed.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.960
And that’s why many Palestinians we’ve spoken to

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:40.680
say the whole idea of reaching some kind of

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.920
two-state solution has been a non-starter for a long time.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.360
It’s a different dynamic that could give Israel

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.440
the political space to forge ahead with annexation.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:20.040
Which many Palestinians expect Israel to do anyway.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.560
Palestinians say it’s about Israel’s track record.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:33.400
That’s something they know well.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:36.800
They don’t see annexation as a moment or a particular date

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.680
but as decades of Israeli policy that have gone unchallenged.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.560
And right now they don’t see that changing.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.280
To find out more about the annexation plans

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.320
I’d recommend visiting Al Jazeera’s website

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:53.640
and clicking on the interactives tab.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:55.720
The AJ Labs team has crunched the numbers

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.760
and put together really informative maps

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.720
that help illustrate what’s going on in the West Bank.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:01.240
I’ll see you all next week.

